\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab O GOD, how often hath Thine ear
\par \pard\li720 To me in willing mercy bowed !
\par While worshipping Thine altar near,
\par Lowly I wept and strongly vowed ;
\par But ah ! The feebleness of man !
\par Have I not vowed and wept in vain ?
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab Return, O Lord of hosts, return !
\par \pard\li720 Behold Thy servant in distress ;
\par My faithlessness again I mourn ;
\par Again forgive my faithlessness ;
\par And to Thine arms my spirit take,
\par And bless me for the Saviour's sake.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab In pity of the soul Thou lov'st,
\par \pard\li720 Now bid the sin Thou hat'st expire ;
\par Let me desire what Thou approv'st,
\par Thou dost approve what I desire ;
\par And Thou wilt deign to call me Thine,
\par And I will dare to call Thee mine.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\tab This day the covenant I sign,
\par \pard\li720 The bond of sure and promised peace ;
\par Nor can I doubt its power divine,
\par Since sealed with Jesu's blood it is :
\par That blood I trust, that blood alone,
\par And make the covenant peace mine own
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.\tab But, that my faith no more may know
\par \pard\li720 Or change, or interval, or end,
\par Help me in all Thy paths to go,
\par And now, as e'er, my voice attend,
\par And gladden me with answers mild,
\par And commune, Father, with Thy child.
\par Amen. 
\par 
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

